          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k18",
          "marks": [
            "k17"
          ],
          "text": "Bali Safari and Marine Park"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k19",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " is about 45 minutes from Sanur and built for kids: a tram safari past lions, elephants, zebras and Komodo dragons, a water-play area, animal shows and a small theme-park zone. International tickets start around "
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1a",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "$38 per person"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1b",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", with packages adding the water park and shows; "
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1d",
          "marks": [
            "k1c"
          ],
          "text": "book online"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1e",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " for the best price and to skip the queue."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k1h",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1g",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Go early to beat the heat, plan on most of the day there, and head back to Sanur for a quiet evening. A private driver waiting for you makes the round trip painless — no negotiating taxis with kids in tow."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k1i",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1j",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Day 3: Move to Ubud and gentle rice terraces"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k1n",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1k",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "After breakfast, transfer up to Ubud (about 60–75 minutes), Bali's green, cultural heart. Keep the first afternoon easy: a short, flat walk at the "
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1l",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Tegalalang Rice Terrace"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1m",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " (kids love the swings and coconut stands) or the Campuhan Ridge Walk early before it warms up, then back to the pool."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k1s",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "k1p",
          "_type": "affiliateLinkRef",
          "placeholderId": "BOOKING_UBUD"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1o",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Choose an Ubud stay with a garden and a good pool — it becomes the family's base for downtime between outings. "
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1q",
          "marks": [
            "k1p"
          ],
          "text": "Search Ubud family stays on Booking.com"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1r",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". Have dinner in central Ubud, which is walkable and relaxed in the evenings."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k1t",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1u",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Day 4: Ubud nature — waterfall, jungle and a swing"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k1y",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1v",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Spend the morning at a family-friendly waterfall such as "
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1w",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Tegenungan"
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1x",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", which has easy steps, a wide pool and a café, or visit the Sacred Monkey Forest (hold small children and keep food hidden). In the afternoon, the Bali jungle swings and nests near Ubud are a hit for photos and giggles, with harnessed options for kids."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k20",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k1z",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "This is a relaxed itinerary, so resist over-scheduling: one main activity plus pool time is plenty for little legs. Keep the late afternoon free for a swim and an early dinner."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k21",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k22",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Day 5: A slow Ubud day"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k24",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k23",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Build in a deliberate rest day — the secret to a happy family trip. Have a lazy breakfast, let the kids swim, and pick just one gentle outing: a short cooking class many families enjoy, a visit to a local market, or feeding the cows and ducks at a rice-field café. Ubud's slower rhythm is ideal for recovering between the bigger days."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "k25",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "k26",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Day 6: Waterbom Bali and move to Nusa Dua"
